WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.100
Do you ever wonder how your rates are spent?

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:11.400
Rates vary across the district depending on
services offered in your area, however on

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.700
average each day a resident will pay $7.33
in rates.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.860
So where does that money go?

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.000
$1.40 a day is spent on our roads and footpaths.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.540
.31c is spent on waste collection and disposal.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.689
.46c goes towards the running of our district’s
libraries.

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:37.160
And 27c helps build and maintain our community
buildings.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.320
15c a day is used for health and safety -

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.640
things like animal control, building consents and cemeteries.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.320
73c is required for planning, governance and
administration costs.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:56.180
Things like Civil Defence, District Development
and Council meetings

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.840
26c is for other.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.980
Miscellaneous costs such as promoting our district’s
economic development

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.440
and contributing towards the Canterbury Museum.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.380
39c is assigned to our swimming pools and
aquatic facilities.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.500
While 17c assists with our ongoing earthquake
recovery.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:25.960
1.39c looks after our waterways, storm water
drains and provides safe, clean drinking water.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.880
It costs another $1 to deal with the sewage.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.560
Leaving 80c a day to maintain our parks, reserves
and sportsgrounds.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.440
So thank you for playing your part in building
and maintaining

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.780
the wonderful Waimakariri District

